namespace pdg { /**

\fn pdg::SpriteLayer::portToLayerVector

\brief adjust the vector to account for the effective camera

Since a vector is relative rather than fixed in coordinate space, this means only rotating it around 0,0 to match the effective camera rotation, and changing the vector length by the camera zoom. The camera translation is not factored in.

\param v Vector in port coordinates

\returns Vector in layer coordinates

**/ }
